{"nodes": [{"id": "cipp_docs_dev_documentation_contributing_to_the_documentation", "label": "Contributing to the Documentation", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CIPP/docs/dev-documentation/contributing-to-the-documentation.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cipp_docs_dev_documentation_contributing_to_the_documentation_gitbook_two_way_sync", "label": "GitBook Two-Way Sync with dev", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CIPP/docs/dev-documentation/contributing-to-the-documentation.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "docs.cipp.app is built from docs/ on the dev branch; GitBook two-way syncs with that branch, so a docs PR must never target main and a local copy goes stale faster than a normal code branch"}, {"id": "cipp_docs_dev_documentation_contributing_to_the_documentation_route_mirrors_ui_path", "label": "User Doc Path Must Mirror UI Route", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CIPP/docs/dev-documentation/contributing-to-the-documentation.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "the in-app speed dial's Check the Documentation entry builds its link by appending the current router path to docs.cipp.app/user-documentation, so a page filed anywhere else is a broken link from inside the product"}, {"id": "cipp_docs_dev_documentation_contributing_to_the_documentation_pages_versus_drawers", "label": "Pages Versus Drawers Rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CIPP/docs/dev-documentation/contributing-to-the-documentation.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "a sub-page is only warranted when a button navigates to a routed page (a file under frontend/src/pages/**); a button that opens a drawer or off-canvas panel is documented inline on the parent page instead"}, {"id": "cipp_docs_dev_documentation_contributing_to_the_documentation_page_anatomy", "label": "User Documentation Page Anatomy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CIPP/docs/dev-documentation/contributing-to-the-documentation.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cipp_docs_dev_documentation_contributing_to_the_documentation_list_and_table_pages_structure", "label": "List and Table Page Structure", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CIPP/docs/dev-documentation/contributing-to-the-documentation.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cipp_docs_dev_documentation_contributing_to_the_documentation_form_and_settings_pages_structure", "label": "Form and Settings Page Structure", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CIPP/docs/dev-documentation/contributing-to-the-documentation.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "cipp_docs_dev_documentation_contributing_to_the_documentation_table_details_convention", "label": "Table Details Convention", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CIPP/docs/dev-documentation/contributing-to-the-documentation.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "if a grid is essentially the raw return of a documented upstream Graph or Exchange object, point at the upstream documentation instead of hand-writing a column table, since it stays correct as that object changes; only write a table when CIPP joins, computes, renames or derives columns"}, {"id": "cipp_docs_dev_documentation_contributing_to_the_documentation_table_actions_convention", "label": "Table Actions HTML Table Convention", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CIPP/docs/dev-documentation/contributing-to-the-documentation.